content.text:
Now CSS. Mobile title and HUD. Add within @media (max-width:700px).

For title:
- `.title-wrap { top: 40%; }` maybe keep 42%.
- show how-to and start-footer.

Need ensure footer doesn't overlap how-to. With 659 height, title-wrap content may end around 560. Footer at bottom 16 top ~610; okay. With taller 844, extra space. How-to after start-actions; margins.

Let's compute title content:
badge ~20, margin 10, title dead 56 + block 65 = 121, tag absolute (no flow), blurb margin 37 + 2 lines 35 = 72, actions margin 18 + button 62 + meta 24 + gap 15 = 119, how-to margin 20+padding 14 + rows (2*44 + gap10)=112. total 20+10+121+72+119+112 = 454. Top = 42% 659=277 - 227 = 50. Bottom = 504. Footer at 610. 100px gap. Could increase how-to padding or add margin-top 28. Fine.

At screenshot current top 42% and content bottom ~460. How-to adds ~112 => 572. Footer ~610. Great.

How-to style:
```
.how-to { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px 10px; width: 100%; margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 13px; }
.how-item { display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; padding: 7px 8px; background: rgba(238,225,199,.04); border: 1px solid rgba(238,225,199,.1); }
.how-item b { font-size: 7.5px; }
.how-item em { font-size: 6.5px; }
.joy-icon, .fire-icon, .hammer-icon, .trap-icon { width: 22px; height:22px; flex:none; }
```
But `.how-to` default `width: max-content`; override width 100%.

Footer:
```
.start-footer { display: flex; gap: 9px; align-items:center; max-width:none; padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(...); }
.start-footer::before { ... hazard strip ... top: -4px? }
.rating-box { width:28;height:28;font-size:20 }
.start-footer p { gap:0; }
.start-footer p b { font-size: 6.5px; letter-spacing:.12em; }
.start-footer p span { font-size: 6.5px; }
.format-tag { display:flex; margin-left:auto; }
.format-tag b { font-size:13px; }
.format-tag span { font-size:5.5px; }
```
The media query currently has `.format-tag { display: none; }` at 900 and `.start-footer { display:none; }` at 700. We'll override in 700 after those declarations in the same media block (order matters). The 700 block already has `.start-footer { display:none; }` line 504, so add new rules later in same block (or modify it). Better edit that line to show and add rules. Also `.how-to { display:none; }` currently line 503; change to grid and add rules. Need place declarations after. We'll edit within block.

Let's make the edits to style.css. Also HUD mobile modifications: edit existing rules.

Current 700 block:
```
.hud-top { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 8px; }
.brand-mini { gap: 5px; }
.brand-mini svg { width: 25px; height: 25px; }
.brand-mini b { font-size: 16px; }
.brand-mini span { display: none; }
.wave-card { width: 145px; }
...
.score-cluster { gap: 5px; }
...
.icon-btn { width: 26px; height: 26px; }
```
Change:
```
.hud-top { display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:space-between; gap:0; }
.brand-mini { ... }
.brand-mini div { display:none; }
.brand-mini svg { width:28; height:28; }
.wave-card { position:absolute; left:50%; top:0; transform:translateX(-50%); width:150px; }
.score-cluster { gap:9px; }
.score-cluster .icon-btn { position:absolute; top:34px; width:26;height:26; }
#pause-btn { right: 31px; } ??? 
```
Need locate relative to hud-top. Buttons are nested in `.score-cluster`; if all ancestors static, absolute containing block = `.hud-top`. `.hud-top` is position:absolute, so yes. But `.score-cluster` if flex is static. Set `.icon-btn { position:absolute; top: 33px; }`; then `#pause-btn { right: 30px; } #mute-btn { right: 0; }`. But top should be relative to hud-top's padding box. hud-top top at safe 14; top 33 -> y 47. Survivor card starts at safe+46=60; wave card ends ~48. So buttons at y 47-73 right side, fine.

Potential overlap with wave card? Wave card spans x 121-271; buttons x ~305-337 and 337-363? At 393 width, safe right 16: mute right 0 relative hud-top right edge at 377 => mute x 351-377; pause right 30 => x 321-347. No overlap.

Score cluster: score-box b 19px, scrap 19px + icon, total maybe 115. Fine.

Hide brand div: `display: none`. The skull icon 28x28. Score + scrap at right. Fine.

But `.hud-top` is grid; to use absolute children we need container position absolute already; set display:block? If display:flex, brand in flow left, wave/score absolute. Let's set `.hud-top { display:block; }` and `.brand-mini { ... }` remains flex. `.score-cluster` absolute right 0 top 0; `.wave-card` absolute left 50%. Actually simpler: position all three absolute. `.brand-mini { position:absolute; left:0; top:0; }`, `.score-cluster { position:absolute; right:0; top:0; }`, `.wave-card { position:absolute; left:50%; top:0; ... }`, `.hud-top { display:block; }`. Need `.hud-top` height not important.

Add mobile survivor card backdrop:
```
.hud-left { top: calc(var(--safe-t) + 54px); gap:7px; }
.survivor-card { padding: 5px 16px 5px 5px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8,10,16,.8), rgba(8,10,16,.42) 70%, transparent); }
```
But barricade panel below already has background. This will make top left readable. However width 39 portrait + gap9 + meta130 + padding 21 = 199; at 393 fits. The wave card center x 121-271; survivor card at x 11-210, overlapping horizontal but y starts 60, wave card ends ~48. Fine.

Score cluster might overlap survivor card if wide? y different.

Ammo cluster bottom 160: Because on mobile viewport 659, joystick at bottom 26+? joystick 122 bottom 26 -> top 511; ammo at bottom 160 -> top ~441; okay. Fine.

"KEEP OUT" decal now smaller/opacity. Good.

Objective bottom 15 max-width 44vw; on mobile action buttons occupy right, objective left-center may overlap joystick? Objective at center bottom 15, width 44vw=173, x 110-283. Joystick x 13-135, action buttons x ~230-377. It might overlap both vertically? joystick top 511, objective bottom 15 => y ~600-640; joystick label at bottom 536? Actually joystick zone height 122, bottom 26 -> top 511, bottom 633. Objective y ~? 15 bottom, height 30 => 614-644, overlapping joystick bottom and fire button bottom. But screenshot shows no objective (maybe fade). It fades after few seconds. Fine. Could move objective to top-center below toast? Not necessary.

Now the `body.touch` class rules at line 458: `.joystick-zone, .action-zone display flex`. But `body.touch .objective bottom 22` good.

Add mobile brand name hidden; but on larger phone landscape (max-height 560) the 700 width query may not apply if width >700. For landscape phones 844x390 width 844, brand text shows and should fit. fine.

Now update mobile title. Let's edit CSS.

