At 320x568:
- The marquee "NOW SHOWING" overlaps the port badge at top left: I see "PS3 CULT CLASSIC REBUILT FOR TOUCH" at y 4, and "NOW SHOWING" at y 24 behind/above? It's cramped. The start-marquee top is safe+2 (16), and title-wrap top 42% of 568 = 238.5 center; content height maybe 500 => top -11! So the badge starts at y ~4, overlapping the marquee at y 16. Indeed the top is clipped/overlapped. This is a real issue on small screens. Need to adjust for short portrait heights. Could add a media query `(max-width: 700px) and (max-height: 700px)` to reduce title sizes/margins or hide how-to/footer. But 659 height was okay-ish; 568 is too short. Since modern phones are 667+ CSS px usually, but iPhone SE 568 is still possible. We should support gracefully.

Options:
- For `max-height: 640px` and portrait, hide the how-to grid and maybe footer to free space, shift title up. But hiding all loses the nice bottom; better shrink.
- Use CSS `@media (max-width: 700px) and (max-height: 640px)`: 
  - `.start-marquee { display: none; }` to avoid overlap (or move top). 
  - `.title-wrap { top: 46%; }`? Hmm content height.
