Let's compute at 320x568 with reduced sizes and no marquee:
port badge starts at y? title-wrap top 50%? If title-wrap centered and content ~400, top 84. Fine. Let's set `top: 47%` maybe. Content: badge 18 + title 50+62=112 + tag + blurb 46 + actions 95 + how-to 100 + margins ~40 => 411. top = 47%*568=267 - 205 = 62. bottom 473. Footer at 520. Good. Should fit.

But setting max-height 640 also affects landscape? landscape is width>700, separate. Good. On 390x659, max-height 640 doesn't apply (659 > 640), so the 659 layout remains. At 320x568, applies. We can use max-height 620 to target 568. But smaller heights may still. Use `(max-width:700px) and (max-height:650px)`.

